        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): mark connected status degraded without bot identity",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen Slack `auth.test` fails at boot, or `channels.slack.botToken` is actually a user token (`xoxp` with `user_id` but no `bot_id`), Socket Mode can still connect while main previously published `healthState: \"healthy\"`. Operators see a connected channel while mention detection is disabled and required-mention rooms fail closed — silent inbound loss.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTransport liveness (`connected: true`) remains useful, but advertising `healthy` is wrong when bot identity is missing under the current bot_id-gated contract (`botUserId = botId ? authUserId : \"\"`). Publish `healthState: \"degraded\"` with `lastError`, and log `slack socket mode connected (degraded identity)`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Misconfigured bot tokens / failed `auth.test` no longer look healthy in channel status.\n- Valid bot-token installs stay `healthy` on connect.\n- App Home slash-command wiring and allowlist-resolution formatting are untouched.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Head SHA:** `204aa27fa823936f88ba69da6fb20d9491165976` (rebased onto current `main`)\n\n### Rank-up coverage\n\n| Rank-up | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Rebase onto current main | done |\n| Provider-path coverage: `user_id` without `bot_id` → degraded | unit test + live Scenario B |\n| Redacted real Slack API / status-path output for healthy-bot, user-token, auth.test-failure | live transcript below |\n| No App Home / resolution-format churn | compare view is 3 files, status-only |\n\n### L1 unit (provider-path)\n\n- `marks socket mode degraded when boot identity is unavailable`\n- `marks socket mode degraded for user_id without bot_id (bot-gated contract)` — mirrors `monitorSlackProvider` auth handling + `formatSlackBotTokenIdentityWarning` + `publishSlackConnectedStatus(..., { degraded: true })`\n\nLocal Vitest in this contributor workspace hit an unrelated `openclaw/plugin-sdk/approval-reference-runtime` resolve failure; CI extension checks are the green gate for this head.\n\n### L3 live Slack API call logs (redacted) — 2026-07-13\n\nUsed live Bot User OAuth Token (`xoxb-…`) and User OAuth Token (`xoxp-…`) from local env only (not committed). **Rotate these tokens — they were pasted into chat.**\n\nPublic/private channel IDs exercised via `conversations.info` (ids redacted below). Full Socket Mode `apps.connections.open` needs App-Level Token `xapp-…` (not provided); proof covers live `auth.test` + channel API + the exact provider identity → `setStatus` / runtime log contract that `onStarted` now calls.\n\n```text\n# Slack live API + status-path proof — PR #105556\nTime (UTC): 2026-07-13T14:07:18.705890+00:00\nTokens: never printed; only kind + last-6 suffix shown.\nIDs/workspace URL/names redacted in this public transcript.\n\n========================================================================\nSCENARIO: A valid bot token (xoxb)\n========================================================================\nAPI: POST https://slack.com/api/auth.test\ntoken: xoxb-…dInXsG  http=200  latency=1147ms\nresponse (redacted):\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"url\": \"https://…REDACTED.slack.com/\",\n  \"team\": \"…REDACTED\",\n  \"user\": \"…REDACTED\",\n  \"team_id\": \"T0B…REDACTED\",\n  \"user_id\": \"U0B…REDACTED\",\n  \"bot_id\": \"B0B…REDACTED\",\n  \"is_enterprise_install\": false\n}\n\nprovider-path identity mirror (current main bot_id-gated contract):\n{\n  \"botUserId_set\": true,\n  \"botId_set\": true,\n  \"authTestFailed\": false,\n  \"authIdentityWarning\": null,\n  \"identityDegraded\": false,\n  \"setStatus\": {\n    \"connected\": true,\n    \"healthState\": \"healthy\",\n    \"lastError\": null\n  },\n  \"runtimeLog\": \"slack socket mode connected\"\n}\nruntime.log => slack socket mode connected\n\n========================================================================\nSCENARIO: B user token misused as botToken (xoxp, user_id without bot_id)\n========================================================================\nAPI: POST https://slack.com/api/auth.test\ntoken: xoxp-…227e0f  http=200  latency=1592ms\nresponse (redacted):\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"url\": \"https://…REDACTED.slack.com/\",\n  \"team\": \"…REDACTED\",\n  \"user\": \"…REDACTED\",\n  \"team_id\": \"T0B…REDACTED\",\n  \"user_id\": \"U0B…REDACTED\",\n  \"is_enterprise_install\": false\n}\n\nprovider-path identity mirror (current main bot_id-gated contract):\n{\n  \"botUserId_set\": false,\n  \"botId_set\": false,\n  \"authTestFailed\": false,\n  \"authIdentityWarning\": \"Slack auth.test identified account \\\"default\\\" as user \\u2026REDACTED without bot_id. channels.slack.botToken, channels.slack.accounts.default.botToken, or SLACK_BOT_TOKEN appears to contain a user token; replace it with a Bot User OAuth Token. Until replaced, explicit bot-mention detection is disabled and required-mention channels fail closed.\",\n  \"identityDegraded\": true,\n  \"setStatus\": {\n    \"connected\": true,\n    \"healthState\": \"degraded\",\n    \"lastError\": \"Slack auth.test identified account \\\"default\\\" as user \\u2026REDACTED without bot_id. channels.slack.botToken, channels.slack.accounts.default.botToken, or SLACK_BOT_TOKEN appears to contain a user token; replace it with a Bot User OAuth Token. Until replaced, explicit bot-mention detection is disabled and required-mention channels fail closed.\"\n  },\n  \"runtimeLog\": \"slack socket mode connected (degraded identity)\"\n}\nruntime.log => slack socket mode connected (degraded identity)\n\n========================================================================\nSCENARIO: C auth.test failure (invalid token)\n========================================================================\nAPI: POST https://slack.com/api/auth.test\ntoken: xoxb-…-proof  http=200  latency=1102ms\nresponse (redacted):\n{\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"error\": \"invalid_auth\"\n}\n\nprovider-path identity mirror (current main bot_id-gated contract):\n{\n  \"botUserId_set\": false,\n  \"botId_set\": false,\n  \"authTestFailed\": true,\n  \"authIdentityWarning\": null,\n  \"identityDegraded\": true,\n  \"setStatus\": {\n    \"connected\": true,\n    \"healthState\": \"degraded\",\n    \"lastError\": \"invalid_auth\"\n  },\n  \"runtimeLog\": \"slack socket mode connected (degraded identity)\"\n}\nruntime.log => slack socket mode connected (degraded identity)\n\n========================================================================\nEXTRA REAL CHANNEL API CALLS (scope/context proof)\n========================================================================\n--- D_bot_conversations.info_public ---\nAPI: POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.info\ntoken: xoxb-…dInXsG  http=200  latency=1155ms\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"channel\": {\n    \"id\": \"C\\u2026REDACTED\",\n    \"is_channel\": true,\n    \"is_private\": false,\n    \"is_member\": true,\n    \"name\": \"\\u2026REDACTED\"\n  }\n}\n\n--- E_bot_conversations.info_private ---\nAPI: POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.info\ntoken: xoxb-…dInXsG  http=200  latency=1408ms\n{\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"error\": \"channel_not_found\"\n}\n\n--- F_user_conversations.info_public ---\nAPI: POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.info\ntoken: xoxp-…227e0f  http=200  latency=1334ms\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"channel\": {\n    \"id\": \"C\\u2026REDACTED\",\n    \"is_channel\": true,\n    \"is_private\": false,\n    \"is_member\": true,\n    \"name\": \"\\u2026REDACTED\"\n  }\n}\n\nNOTE: Full Socket Mode (apps.connections.open) needs App-Level Token xapp-… which was not provided;\nthis proof uses live auth.test + conversations.info plus the exact provider identity→setStatus/log contract.\nBEFORE (main): onStarted always publishSlackConnectedStatus() => healthState=healthy even when identityDegraded.\nAFTER (PR): onStarted publishSlackConnectedStatus(..., {degraded:true}) when identityDegraded.\n```\n\n### Before / after contract\n\n| Case | Live `auth.test` | BEFORE (`main` onStarted) | AFTER (this PR) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Valid `xoxb` (has `bot_id`) | ok + bot_id | `healthState: healthy` | `healthState: healthy` + log `slack socket mode connected` |\n| `xoxp` as botToken (`user_id`, no `bot_id`) | ok, no bot_id | still `healthy` (bug) | `healthState: degraded` + `lastError` warning + log `… (degraded identity)` |\n| Invalid token | `invalid_auth` | still `healthy` (bug) | `healthState: degraded` + `lastError: invalid_auth` |\n\n### Files\n\n- `extensions/slack/src/monitor/provider-support.ts` — degraded option on `publishSlackConnectedStatus`\n- `extensions/slack/src/monitor/provider.ts` — `identityDegraded` gate on Socket `onStarted`\n- `extensions/slack/src/monitor/provider.reconnect.test.ts` — healthy / missing-identity / user-without-bot_id coverage\n\n## Agent Transcript\n\n- Cursor session: Slack L3 live identity/status API proof (tokens redacted; rotate if exposed).\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n",
